anyone who gets to play spider-man is  living a dream come true  unfortunately for Andrew Garfield that  dream was brief why was this tenure as  Peter Parker so short the answer as  always is complicated the best  characters often come from actors with a  concrete vision who can turn stories  experiences and research into a coherent  whole  Garfield believed in the power of this  process as fervently as a 25 year old  rookie actor could after the series  cancellation he told the Guardian about  the work he put in behind the scenes to  do right by the character I thought if I  can infuse all this ancient knowledge  and wisdom into spider-man  it could be profoundly affecting for  young people in the audience that was  always my intention and what I tried to  do  unfortunately the studio didn't agree  the cutting of character centric scenes  the promotion of Garfield as a celebrity  and the ultimate reality of the amazing  spider-man as a blockbuster series made  Garfield's highbrow ideas unsustainable  he has at least made peace with this  rift telling The Guardian in the same  interview what I'll proudly say is that  I didn't compromise who I was I was only  ever myself Andrew Garfield is an  actor's actor man that means he was  never going to be satisfied working  entirely in superhero blockbusters ever  since Tom Holland took up the web suit  to flip and quip his way through the MCU  sprawling saga Garfield has devoted  himself almost entirely to cerebral art  house cinema 2016 saw him take part in  Martin Scorsese's silence in which he  played a 17th century Jesuit priest in  2017 he played a polio survivor in the  biopic read most recently he starred in  under the Silverlake a neon noir that  takes his character across Los Angeles  in pursuit of conspiracy at the end of  spider-man pushed Garfield into this  kind of work it's as much a blessing as  it is a curse and perhaps Garfield  himself feels the same way Peter Parker  is a consummate nerd in his debut and  amazing fantasy number 15 he's bitten by  a radioactive spider because he's  visiting a lab after school Peter Parker  just loves science so dearly that he  likes to spend his time discussing the  finer points of atomic energy Cristian  Midtown highs only professional  Wallflower on the very first panel he  ever appeared in he's a geek before he  ever gets the power to climb walls and  swing across New York sure the Amazing  Spider  man movies informants of Peters nerdery  but what we actually see looks very  different of the three actors who make  up Spidey's big screen presence Garfield  is the one who's handsome looks weren't  toned down at all  Garfield's Peter Parker skateboards and  broods with a charisma that's entirely  too cool Maguire Spidey loved to talk  chemistry and hollands gets together  with his best friend Ned to build Lego  models of the Death Star but you can't  really picture Garfield spider-man doing  much in the geek arena beyond maybe  playing the occasional round of Mortal  Kombat he's just too cool and when it  comes to spider-man that's a fatal flaw  the MCU debuted in 2008 with the  explosive arrival of Robert Downey jr.  Tony Stark and Iron Man by 2012 Marvel  Studios had pulled its team together in  the Avengers a blockbuster event that  would usher in what we might just one  day call the Marvel Age of movies and oh  yeah Spiderman was there too of course  with Sony holding the movie rights to  the character he remained trapped in his  own cinematic universe though amazing  spider-man did well at the box office  the fact remained that it was completely  eclipsed by the other Marvel based movie  to come out that year plus the MCU is  demonstrating far more staying power  than Sony Spider flicks in retrospect  the writing was very much on the wall  people were loving Marvel's son equipped  latent vision of their own universe far  more than Sony's slick take on the  iconic webslinger as the years went on  Marvel built up more and more gravity  and spider-man the company's flagship  comic book hero was pulled in and  revamped by Tom Holland there was an  inevitability to this process not even  the best movie could afford it and  unfortunately Garfield's films were far  from the best director Sam Raimi spin on  spider-man feels like ancient history  now but try not to let the memories of  Tobey Maguire dancing in the jazz club  cloud your mind just yet instead  remember alfred molinos trailblazing  performance as a villain at war with  himself  remember Willem Dafoe's lunatic glee at  being able to bombard spider-man with  pumpkin themed bombs  you in or are you out it's you who's out  Gaby out of your mind  remember kirsten dunst is warm-hearted  girl next door remember the upside-down  kiss and perhaps above all remember that  iconic train rescue at the time the  world loved those movies only five years  separate the last of the McGuire trilogy  from the first of the Garfield duo in  some ways that's a long time but it's  not long enough for a generation to turn  over most kids who grew up with McGuire  were barely into adulthood by the time  Garfield rolled around McGuire remained  an a-list star rather than an elder  statesman passing down a beloved role it  was too soon for anyone to erase the  mark left by the first trilogy from  their minds too soon for there to be an  organic desire for a new take on an old  favorite and in the end that's the  desire a superhero flick lives and dies  by check out one of our newest videos  right here plus even more looper videos  about spider-man are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you  [Music]
 

